Highly Available Web Application on AWS
Self-directed · VPC, EC2, ALB, Auto Scaling, IAM, VPC Endpoints

-Provisioned an Auto Scaling group with two EC2 instances in VPC private subnets in two AZs, ALB nodes in the public subnets, 
and a security group allowing traffic from the ALB to the instances.
-Reduced cost by configuring an S3 gateway endpoint instead of a NAT gateway so that the instances could still fetch the Amazon 
Linux repo packages and website files from S3.
-Traced a curl timeout to the Amazon Linux repos in the system logs to an S3 endpoint associated with the wrong route table and 
re-associated it with the private subnet's route table.
-Resolved a TCP connection timeout to the ALB after having confirmed DNS resolved and curl was hanging, isolating 
the cause to routing which led to checking the route table and finding an IGW route to 0.0.0.0/16 instead of 0.0.0.0/0.
-Tested availability by terminating one instance and viewing the ASG activity history and target group health checks as another 
instance was launched and passed.


